          "guid": "mt1b3qy3f8z8jwzn",
          "message": {
            "text": "CBDT promotion is driven by the selected glyph representation because CSSOM Range geometry exposes the advance and line box, not the embedded strike's ink bounds. The Linux helper-backed route probe selected Noto Color Emoji and classified its glyphs as bitmap correctly, while the per-glyph clip visibly removed strike pixels; capturing the containing line fragment preserves Chromium's exact paint without inspecting the platform, family name, or Unicode value.",
            "markdown": "CBDT promotion is driven by the selected glyph representation because CSSOM Range geometry exposes the advance and line box, not the embedded strike's ink bounds. The Linux helper-backed route probe selected Noto Color Emoji and classified its glyphs as bitmap correctly, while the per-glyph clip visibly removed strike pixels; capturing the containing line fragment preserves Chromium's exact paint without inspecting the platform, family name, or Unicode value."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/capture/emoji.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 656,
                  "endLine": 676,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "            // CBDT/CBLC glyphs are strike bitmaps whose ink bounds are not\n            // exposed by CSSOM Range geometry. Chromium/Skia may paint the\n            // strike outside the character advance (Noto Color Emoji does on\n            // Linux), so clipping a per-glyph screenshot to that Range loses\n            // real pixels. Until the helper transports the selected strike's\n            // bitmap metrics, preserve Chromium's paint ownership by\n            // screenshotting this one line fragment as the established\n            // segment-level raster boundary. This is keyed to the selected\n            // glyph representation, never to a platform, font name, or\n            // codepoint.\n            if (selected.some((span) => span.representation === \"bitmap\")) {\n              const rect = { x: seg.x, y: seg.y, width: seg.width, height: seg.height };\n              seg.rasterRect = rect;\n              seg.rasterGlyphs = structural.length > 0 ? structural : undefined;\n              candidates.push({\n                rect,\n                key: `seg-bitmap|${seg.text}|${seg.color ?? \"\"}|${seg.fontSize ?? \"\"}|${seg.fontWeight ?? \"\"}|${rect.width}x${rect.height}`,\n                setDataUri: (uri) => { seg.rasterDataUri = uri; },\n                snapRectToClip: true,\n              });\n              continue;"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
